Feature: Waypoints
  When PLAN is selected, each click on the map adds a [[waypoint]] at the end of the plan, at
  the [[plan altitude]]. A right-click removes the last item, and CLEAR removes all items.
  The map shows the plan as a dashed line, and the mission on the vehicle as a solid line.

  Expectation: A click adds a waypoint
    Given the map tool is PLAN
    When the operator clicks the map
    Then the plan goes up by 1
    And the last plan item is WAYPOINT
    And the newest waypoint is at the plan altitude

  Expectation: Right-click removes the last item
    Given the map tool is PLAN
    And the plan has at least 1 item
    When the operator right-clicks the map
    Then the plan goes down by 1

  Expectation: Right-click on an empty plan does nothing
    Given the map tool is PLAN
    And the plan has 0 items
    When the operator right-clicks the map
    Then the plan stays the same

  Expectation: CLEAR empties the plan
    When the operator clears the plan
    Then the plan has 0 items
    And the takeoff is not planned

  Expectation: A full plan takes no more waypoints
    ArduPilot keeps approximately 650 mission items in its memory, so the plan stops at 650.
    With BRD_SD_MISSION and an SD card, ArduPilot keeps more.
    Overrides: A click adds a waypoint
    Given the map tool is PLAN
    And the plan has 650 items
    When the operator clicks the map
    Then the plan stays the same

  Expectation: An empty plan has no last item
    Docs: hidden
    Given the plan has 0 items
    Then the last plan item is none
